@startuml
title UML State Chart Diagram

[*] --> PoweringOn

state "Powering On" as PoweringOn
PoweringOn : entry / Start power-on sequence
PoweringOn : do / Check if everything is working
PoweringOn : exit / Transition to Startup Check or stop system

state "Startup Check" as StartupCheck
StartupCheck : entry / Perform startup checks
StartupCheck : do / Check for problems
StartupCheck : exit / Transition to Ready To Use or stop system

state "Ready To Use" as ReadyToUse
ReadyToUse : entry / System is ready
ReadyToUse : do / Allow user actions
ReadyToUse : exit / Stay in state

state "Monitoring" as Monitoring
Monitoring : entry / Start monitoring
Monitoring : do / Monitor sensors
Monitoring : exit / Stay in state

state "Alarm Activated" as AlarmActivated
AlarmActivated : entry / Activate alarm and send alerts
AlarmActivated : do / Handle false alarms or time end
AlarmActivated : exit / Transition to False Alarm, Time Ended, or Ready To Use

state "False Alarm" as FalseAlarm
FalseAlarm : entry / System returns to normal after false alarm check
FalseAlarm : do / Return to Monitoring state
FalseAlarm : exit / Stay in state

state "Time Ended" as TimeEnded
TimeEnded : entry / System returns to normal after time ends
TimeEnded : do / Return to Ready To Use state
TimeEnded : exit / Stay in state

PoweringOn --> StartupCheck : Power-On
StartupCheck --> ReadyToUse : Startup Complete
ReadyToUse --> Monitoring : Activation Requested
Monitoring --> AlarmActivated : Sensor Triggered
AlarmActivated --> FalseAlarm : False Alarm Check
AlarmActivated --> TimeEnded : Time Ends
FalseAlarm --> ReadyToUse : Password Entered
TimeEnded --> ReadyToUse : Password Entered

@enduml
